course: dictionary
lesson: 15779
title: Twofold: two parts or twice as much
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Twofold is a word with two meanings. It can mean something has two parts or two sides, or it can mean twice as much or twice as many. The words around it show you which one. «The problem is twofold: we have no money and no time.» The sentence names two problems, so twofold means two parts.
explain: «Sales rose twofold after the new shop opened.» Rose twofold means the sales doubled, so they became twice as big. Always ask: is the writer naming parts, or comparing an amount? If you can count the parts, it means two parts. If an amount doubles, it means twice as much.
explain: Twofold can be an adjective, as in «a twofold problem», or an adverb, as in «increase twofold». Both come from the same idea of two. To check your meaning, swap in "two" or "double" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Twofold means having two parts or two sides.
fact: Twofold also means twice as much or twice as many.
fact: «The reason is twofold» means there are two reasons.
fact: «A twofold increase» means the amount doubles.
fact: Twofold is often used in maths, science and formal writing.
exercise: «The plan has a twofold purpose: to save money and to help the town.» What does twofold mean here? | Half the size | Very quick | *Two parts | Brightly coloured
exercise: «Our water bill rose twofold this year.» What does twofold mean? | Quite quiet | *Twice as much | Half as much | Very cold
exercise: «The reason for the delay is twofold.» How many reasons does this sentence give? | Three | One | None | *Two
test: «Her answer was twofold: she said yes, and she also offered to help.» What does twofold mean here? | *Two parts | Very loud | Hidden | Twice as tall
test: «The number of visitors increased twofold in one year.» What does increased twofold mean? | The number stayed the same | *The number doubled | The number halved | The number was hidden
exam: The school's plan is twofold, with two clear goals for the year. What does twofold mean in this sentence? | Half as big | *Having two parts | Lost forever | Very slow
